<title>Ethylene Glycol Toxicity: Diagnosis.</title>
<graphic href="eee0590-w001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Patient unconscious or signs&#x002F;symptoms of unknown ingestion. Obtain serum chemistry, serum osmolality, and arterial blood gases. Calculate anion gap and osmolal gap.</label>
<path target="cell-2">Metabolic acidosis with anion gap</path>
<path target="cell-3">Metabolic acidosis without anion gap, or no metabolic acidosis</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Serum osmolal gap present?</label>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-3">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Perform urinalysis and&#x002F;or Wood's lamp evaluation. Calcium oxalate crystals present and&#x002F;or fluorescence of urine?</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-3">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-6">
<label>Send for serum levels of ethylene glycol, methanol, isopropyl alcohol, and ethanol.</label>
<path target="cell-7">Ethylene glycol positive</path>
<path target="cell-8">Methanol positive</path>
<path target="cell-9">Ethanol positive</path>
<path target="cell-10">Isopropyl alcohol positive</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Ethylene glycol ingestion.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Methanol ingestion.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>Ethanol ingestion.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-10">
<label>Isopropyl alcohol ingestion.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Ethylene glycol ingestion unlikely. High index of suspicion for ingestion?</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-11">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>Consider other diagnoses.</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>Anion gap &#x003D; Na &#x2212; (Cl<sub>&#x2212;</sub> + HCO<sub>3&#x2212;</sub>) &#x003D; [Normal 8-12]</footnote>
<footnote>Osmolal gap &#x003D; Measured serum osmoles &#x2212; Calculated serum osmols &#x003D; Measured serum osmoles &#x2212; (2(Na) + BUN &#x002F;2.8 + Glucose&#x002F;18 &#x003D; [Normal &lt;10]</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
